### Explanation

- [h]Amplitude[/h]: The amplitude of the sine wave is [c]2[/c], which means the wave reaches a maximum of 2 and a minimum of -2.
- [u]Period[/u]: The period of the sine wave is $2\pi$, which is the distance between two consecutive peaks or troughs.
- [b]Key Points[/b]:
  - At $x = 0$, $y = 0$ (the wave starts at the origin).
  - At $x = \frac{\pi}{2}$, $y = 2$ (the maximum value).
  - At $x = \pi$, $y = 0$ (the wave crosses the x-axis).
  - At $x = \frac{3\pi}{2}$, $y = -2$ (the minimum value).
  - At $x = 2\pi$, $y = 0$ (the wave completes one full cycle).
